# SPIKE Prime over Web Bluetooth

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:ex_spike, github: "ErikMejerHansen/ex_spike"},
  {:kino_web_bluetooth, github: "ErikMejerHansen/kino_web_bluetooth"}
])
```

## About

This notebook talks to a LEGO® SPIKE™ Prime hub from Livebook.
[KinoWebBluetooth](https://github.com/ErikMejerHansen/kino_web_bluetooth)
carries the bytes over your browser's Web Bluetooth, and
[ExSPIKE](https://github.com/ErikMejerHansen/ex_spike) turns them into
messages.

You need a Chromium based browser (Chrome, Edge) and a hub running the
SPIKE App 3 firmware. Press the hub's Bluetooth button so it advertises.

> ExSPIKE and KinoWebBluetooth are not affiliated with, sponsored,
> authorized or endorsed by The LEGO Group. LEGO® and SPIKE™ are
> trademarks of The LEGO Group.

## Connect

Evaluate the Smart Cell below, click **Connect** and pick your hub. The
service UUID is already set to the SPIKE Prime service.

